    "field": "Climate change",
    "problem": "Climate studies have extensively focused on mean and extreme precipitation, but precipitation variability has received less attention and is often assumed to be static, hindering a complete understanding of the hydrologic cycle's response to warming and its societal impacts.",
    "method": "The study quantifies changes in precipitation variability by calculating its standard deviation across multiple timescales in three climate model ensembles, comparing a late 20th-century baseline to a late 21st-century warming scenario, and examining observational station data for consistency.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the change in precipitation variability with warming across daily to decadal timescales using global climate model simulations and station observations.",
